      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "OX KNOX (5) is back from a break of nine weeks and looks to be right up to the mark following a recent trial win. Will have plenty of admirers. DONA AMALIA (7) has been close to the mark of late and again performed impressively at the most recent appearance, making up plenty of ground but finding one better over 1690m at Shepparton. Will need a bit of luck negotiating a very wide starting position. Needs to be at her best to beat this field but she good enough to play a major role. KISS AT MIDNIGHT (8) did a good job to finish in the minor placings two runs back then things went sour last time when she broke and finished a long way back in seventh over 2080m at Cranbourne. No harm in drawing here with the sprint lane to rely upon. Meets a similar line up so if she behaves a big run is likely. MISTA WALKER (4) is racing very well of late, finishing in the money two runs back then scoring over 2080m at Cranbourne last time out. In the mix.",
